    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ddd43cac-6ae5-546e-b0db-53cfc8607617",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y &=0 \\\\ x-y &=0 \\\\ x-y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent dependent.",
